{"title":"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that one of every 500 people in a certain population has a particular disease, which displays no symptoms. A blood test is available for screening for this disease. For a person who has this disease, the test always turns out positive. For a person who does not have the disease, however, there is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/0/0b04a3bd51b4c6a454c3aae545a1dbc6a5bff05d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"23\" height=\"14\" /> false positive rate--in other words, for such people, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/6/30696f72e40dac44ba3d77958f23e54518505ca9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$98\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of the time the test will turn out negative, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/0/0b04a3bd51b4c6a454c3aae545a1dbc6a5bff05d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"23\" height=\"14\" /> of the time the test will turn out positive and will incorrectly indicate that the person has the disease. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be the probability that a person who is chosen at random from this population and gets a positive test result actually has the disease. Which of the following is closest to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/6/02635f12f403b891c26538073d75aeefe31ef18b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{98}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{9}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{1}{11}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{49}{99}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{98}{99}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"404\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This question can be solved by considering all the possibilities:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> out of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/9/a39b14023c98c943554d150561aacc188c4ce26d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$500$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> people will have the disease and will be tested positive for the disease.\n</p><p>Out of the remaining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/0/6500248a8e3334fcfb20b237b0e343980327ad17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$499$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> people, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/2/3423afe40eb71ccb8b9d670383b3c5af8a82e75f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{50}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />, or about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> people, will be tested positive for the disease incorrectly.\n</p><p>Therefore, an approximation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> can be found by taking <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/9/3e9630ce91dd15ad13750f7f6061e9fe403763d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{1 +10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"55\" height=\"40\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/a/22afcbc99797f29eaa84c1dbf30bf0670acc30d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fffc7368e8e7b77c88b0b4bf732c88c60e27b439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This question can also be solved by using a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/2/6325a27e1b67d110bb8f0aafbed2e1c3e2d60992.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{probability1}{probability2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"101\" height=\"43\" /> solution. \n</p><p>If the test is positive there are two cases: (1) The person was true-positive (2) The person was false-positive\n</p><p>For the first case, the probability of the person being true-positive is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/b/82b7bf02eac53496952c04e63a95129968725abd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{500}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"29\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>For the second case, the probability of the person being false-positive is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/4/1d4ce52a82d7eddf6f56f171a455275bf0cf30f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{499}{500}\\cdot\\dfrac{1}{50}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>The probability of the test being positive is the sum of these values, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/3/aa33af020cccf7df745109354dcae093123428c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{549}{25000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"51\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>The final probability will be in the form: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/8/7b8c14535d1b06256ed23155206f22359f89b597.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{P(true positive)}{P(positive)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"132\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>Plugging in the values we get: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/0/4a0fedc436eae7a04d6b66acee8e3b97e682f86e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{\\dfrac{1}{500}}{\\dfrac{549}{25000}}=\\dfrac{50}{549}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -35px\" width=\"111\" height=\"80\" /> This fraction is clearly closest to  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/a/22afcbc99797f29eaa84c1dbf30bf0670acc30d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fffc7368e8e7b77c88b0b4bf732c88c60e27b439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To solve this problem, you need to find the probability of a correctly identified positive and divided by the total probability of a positive. \n</p><p>The probability of obtaining a correctly identified positive is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/b/82b7bf02eac53496952c04e63a95129968725abd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{500}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"29\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>The probability of obtaining an incorrectly identified positive is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/8/ee8a85b138bc3384b0c1f14051095f04522320d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{2}{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"38\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/6/8d69b10fd847227aceecd5cc71cd6c1b1be35396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{10}{500}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/b/82b7bf02eac53496952c04e63a95129968725abd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{500}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"29\" height=\"37\" /> + <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/6/8d69b10fd847227aceecd5cc71cd6c1b1be35396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{10}{500}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"38\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/d/06d7099150b4603ec000dfa342445581ce6af9fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{11}{500}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"38\" /> = the probability of obtaining a positive.\n</p><p>Correctly identifed positive / positive = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/b/82b7bf02eac53496952c04e63a95129968725abd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{500}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"29\" height=\"37\" /> / <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/d/06d7099150b4603ec000dfa342445581ce6af9fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{11}{500}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"38\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/a/22afcbc99797f29eaa84c1dbf30bf0670acc30d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fffc7368e8e7b77c88b0b4bf732c88c60e27b439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/igGLCogR-dk\">https://youtu.be/igGLCogR-dk</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B\">2012 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017225745\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.039 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.060 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 269/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2324/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6251/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.179      1 -total\n 60.52%    7.976      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 38.50%    5.074      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:10800:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017225745 and revision id 263588. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}